Theorem RL-34: pre-tail-call ownership handoff or release

  Preconditions:
    - The callee parameter Access is Owned or Borrowed.

  Soundness property:
    Owned -> HandoffBeforeTail.
    Borrowed -> ReleaseBeforeTail.
    No logical release follows the tail call. A projection may realize the
    action by any mechanism that preserves evaluator behavior and TCO.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate both Access cases. Coverage gate: 2 actions.
    Negative-direction witness: a post-tail-call release is rejected.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl34_tail_call_preservation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-34 freezes handoff-before-tail for Owned and release-before-tail for Borrowed, never a post-call release
